# Situation Relationship Directive

**SoT:** [`docs/02-product/solenos-situation-relationship-directive.md`](../../docs/02-product/solenos-situation-relationship-directive.md)

## Principle

Do **not** decide same vs new situation by keywords alone. Evaluate whether new input **changes understanding of an existing care reality**.

Job = relationships between life changes — **not** grouping notes into piles.

## Pipeline

Capture → Context Analysis → **Situation Relationship Engine** → UPDATE / NEW_RELATED / NEW_UNRELATED / ADDITIONAL_CONTEXT / UNCERTAIN → Living Care Record

## Signals (ordered)

1. Time relationship  
2. Same care recipient  
3. Topic/underlying issue (not keywords)  
4. Answers an open uncertainty → update same  
5. Strengthens a pattern → same thread  
6. New decision → **NEW_RELATED_EVENT** linked, not merged  

## Caregiver

Never make them manage architecture. Do **not** ask “Is this a new situation?” every turn — only on meaningful `UNCERTAIN_NEEDS_REVIEW`.

## Situation Graph

ACS = current focus. Full reality = graph (situations + linked events). Engine confidence labels are internal only — never % or enums in caregiver UI.
